    <body>
      <div type="clause" n="28">
        <head><ref type="lawCode" target="law:Ine">Ine</ref> 28</head>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="28" corresp="#wit-e"><pb n="100" ed="#liebermann"/>LXXII. Se<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="30" target="#Ine_28.lnote.oe.30"/> ðeof gefehð<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="31" target="#Ine_28.lnote.oe.31"/>, ah X<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="32" target="#Ine_28.lnote.oe.32"/> scill., ⁊ se cyning ðone ðeof; ⁊ þa mægas<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="33" target="#Ine_28.lnote.oe.33"/> him swerian aðas unfæhða.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="28" corresp="#wit-h"><pb n="100" ed="#liebermann"/>LXXII. Se (þe<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="4" target="#Ine_28.lnote.oe.4"/>) ðeof gefehð, he ah X scll', ⁊ se cyning þone ðeof; ⁊ þa magas him swerian aþas unfehþa.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="28" corresp="#wit-b-no-prol"><pb n="100" ed="#liebermann"/>Be ðeowes mannes onfenge æt ðyfðe. Se ðe ðeof gefehð, he ah tyn scill', ⁊ se cyning ðone ðeof; ⁊ ða magas him swerian aðas unfæðða.<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="7" target="#Ine_28.lnote.oe.7"/></ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="la" source="#liebermann" n="28" corresp="#wit-q"><pb n="101" ed="#liebermann"/>Qui furem ceperit, habeat inde<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="24" target="#Ine_28.lnote.oe.24"/> decem<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="25" target="#Ine_28.lnote.oe.25"/> solidos, et rex ipsum furem; et parentes eius abiurent<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="26" target="#Ine_28.lnote.oe.26"/> ei<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="27" target="#Ine_28.lnote.oe.27"/> factionem.</ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="ang" source="#attenborough" corresp="#wit-e"><pb n="44" ed="#attenborough"/>[Be ðeowes mannes onfenge æt ðyfðe.] Se [þe]<ptr type="editorNote" n="7" target="#Ine_28.attnote.fn.7"/> ðeof gefehð, [he]<ptr type="editorNote" n="7" target="#Ine_28.attnote.fn.7-2"/> ah X scill., ⁊ se cyning ðone ðeof; ⁊ þa mægas him swerian aðas unfæhða.</ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="ang" source="#jurasinski-and-oliver" n="28" corresp="#wit-e"><pb n="394" ed="#jurasinski-and-oliver"/>{LXXII} Se ðeof gefehð, ah X sciƚƚ, ⁊ se cyning ðone ðeof; ⁊ þa mægas him swerian aðas unfæhða.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="de" source="#liebermann"><pb n="101" ed="#liebermann"/>Wer<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="1" target="#Ine_28.lnote.de.1"/> einen Dieb [bei der That<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="2" target="#Ine_28.lnote.de.2"/>] fängt, [der<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="3" target="#Ine_28.lnote.de.3"/>] erhält 10 Schill.<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="4" target="#Ine_28.lnote.de.4"/>, und der König den Dieb<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="5" target="#Ine_28.lnote.de.5"/>; und die Verwandten [des Diebes] sollen jenem [Einfänger] Urfehde-Eide<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="6" target="#Ine_28.lnote.de.6"/> schwören.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude" ana="#fromGerman">Whoever catches a thief [in the act] receives 10 shillings, and the king the thief; and the kinsmen [of the thief] are to swear oaths of renouncing feud to that [captor].</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#attenborough" corresp="#wit-e"><pb n="45" ed="#attenborough"/>He who captures a thief shall have 10 shillings. The thief shall be given up to the king, and his kinsmen shall swear that they will carry on no vendetta against him<ptr type="editorNote" n="1" target="#Ine_28.attnote.n.1"/>.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#whitelock"><pb n="402" ed="#whitelock"/>He who captures a thief has a right to 10 shillings, and the king to the thief; and the kinsmen are to swear to him oaths that they will wage no feud.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#jurasinski-and-oliver" corresp="#wit-e"><pb n="395" ed="#jurasinski-and-oliver"/>He who catches a thief receives 10 shillings, and the king the thief; and his kinsmen swear oaths to renounce feuding.</ab>
        <note type="comparison" source="#wormald-ppmel" n="127"><label>something like</label> <ref target="clause:Wi_25">Wi 25–27</ref> <quote>Something like the royal discretion of Wi. 25–7, p. 14, may be implied by Ine 28</quote></note>
        <note type="comparison" source="#jurasinski-and-oliver" n="394"><label>cf.</label> <ref target="clause:Ine_12">Ine 12</ref> <quote>Hapax legomenon. Cf. §12.</quote></note>
        <note type="comparison" source="#jurasinski-and-oliver" n="394"><label>equivalent phrase</label> <ref target="clause:Ine_35">Ine 35</ref> <quote>The phrase aðas unfæhða is equivalent to the unceases áð of §35.</quote></note>
        <note type="comparison" source="#jurasinski-and-oliver" n="395"><label>compare</label> <ref target="clause:Wi_26">Wi 26–26.1</ref> <quote>Compare Wihtred §21–21.1 [L26–26.1].</quote></note>
        <note type="comparison" source="#jurasinski-and-oliver" n="395"><label>cf.</label> <ref target="clause:Ine_17">Ine 17</ref> <quote>Likely the meldfeoh ("reward due an informant") discussed in §17; this may also apply to [...] §20.</quote></note>
        <note type="comparison" source="#jurasinski-and-oliver" n="395"><label>cf.</label> <ref target="clause:Ine_20">Ine 20</ref> <quote>Likely the meldfeoh ("reward due an informant") discussed in §17; this may also apply to [...] §20.</quote></note>
        <note type="comparedBy" source="#jurasinski-and-oliver" n="383"><label>cf.</label> <ref target="clause:Ine_17">Ine 17</ref> <quote>The reward may well be equivalent to the 10 shillings for a person who turns in a thief described in §28.</quote></note>
        <note type="comparedBy" source="#jurasinski-and-oliver" n="385"><label>compare</label> <ref target="clause:Ine_20">Ine 20</ref> <quote>Compare §28, which allows a 10-shilling reward to one who captures a thief.</quote></note>
        <note type="comparedBy" source="#jurasinski-and-oliver" n="400"><label>equivalent phrase</label> <ref target="clause:Ine_35">Ine 35</ref> <quote>The phrase unceases áð is equivalent to the aðas unfæhða of §28.</quote></note>
        <note type="comparedBy" source="#jurasinski-and-oliver" n="402"><label>compare</label> <ref target="clause:Ine_36">Ine 36</ref> <quote>Compare to §28.</quote></note>
        <note type="comparedBy" source="#jurasinski-and-oliver" n="432"><label>compare</label> <ref target="clause:Ine_72">Ine 72</ref> <quote>Compare to §28.</quote></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Ine_28.lnote.oe.7" n="7" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">100</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">später geänd. in</hi> -ægða</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">later altered to -ægða</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Ine_28.lnote.oe.24" n="24" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">101</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">fehlt Co Or</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">lacking in Co Or</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Ine_28.lnote.oe.25" n="25" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">101</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">so Lond;</hi> s. d. <hi rend="italic">übrige</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">thus Lond; s. d. the others</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Ine_28.lnote.oe.26" n="26" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">101</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">iurent ei iuramentum, <hi rend="italic">ohne</hi> fa. <hi rend="italic">Lond;</hi> uel faccionem <hi rend="italic">übergeschr. Co, im Texte Or</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">iurent ei iuramentum, without fa. Lond; uel faccionem written above Co, in the text Or</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Ine_28.lnote.oe.27" n="27" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">101</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">verbessert aus</hi> eum <hi rend="italic">M</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">corrected from eum M</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Ine_28.lnote.oe.4" n="4" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">100</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">übergeschr.</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">written above</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Ine_28.lnote.oe.30" n="30" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">100</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">ðe <hi rend="italic">fügt zu Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">ðe added by Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Ine_28.lnote.oe.31" n="31" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">100</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">he <hi rend="italic">fügt zu Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">he added by Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Ine_28.lnote.oe.32" n="32" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">100</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">tyn <hi rend="italic">Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">tyn Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Ine_28.lnote.oe.33" n="33" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">100</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">magas <hi rend="italic">Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">magas Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="Ine_28.lnote.de.1" n="1" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">72</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">3</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">H cor. und B modernisieren</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">H cor. and B modernise</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="Ine_28.lnote.de.2" n="2" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">73</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">1</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">S. o.</hi> 12; <hi rend="italic">vgl.</hi> handhaft 11. Dass den Verbrecher Leibesstrafe traf oder bedrohte, beweist Urfehde</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude"><hi rend="italic">See above</hi> 12; <hi rend="italic">cf.</hi> handhaft 11. That corporal punishment befell or threatened the criminal is proved by the Urfehde</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="Ine_28.lnote.de.3" n="3" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">72</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">3</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">H cor. und B modernisieren</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">H cor. and B modernise</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="Ine_28.lnote.de.4" n="4" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">73</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">1</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">Vgl. Gl</hi> Anzeige 4</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude"><hi rend="italic">Cf. Gl</hi> Anzeige 4</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="Ine_28.lnote.de.5" n="5" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">73</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">1</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">‘Der gebundene Dieb gehört dem Richter, nicht dem Bestohlenen’ (Brunner II 485. 579) auch bei and. Germ. <hi rend="italic">Vgl. Gl</hi>-Abfindung 1. In Kent scheint, laut des grösseren Anteils des Verletzten am Diebe (Wi 26), die königliche Gerichtsgewalt geringer</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">‘The bound thief belongs to the judge, not to the man robbed’ (Brunner II 485. 579) among other Germanic peoples too. <hi rend="italic">Cf. Gl</hi>-Abfindung 1. In Kent, to judge from the injured party’s larger share in the thief (Wi 26), the king’s judicial authority seems to have been smaller</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="Ine_28.lnote.de.6" n="6" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">73</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">1</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">Vgl. Gl</hi> Blutrache 140; Urfehde. Gen. plur. <hi rend="italic">fæhða</hi> auch Epos <hi rend="italic">Crist</hi> 617. Q braucht Nordfz. <hi rend="italic">factio</hi> für ‘Fehde’ auch sonst; <hi rend="italic">s. Wb</hi> und Ducange</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude"><hi rend="italic">Cf. Gl</hi> Blutrache 140; Urfehde. Gen. pl. <hi rend="italic">fæhða</hi> also in the epic <hi rend="italic">Crist</hi> 617. Q uses North French <hi rend="italic">factio</hi> for ‘feud’ elsewhere too; <hi rend="italic">see Wb</hi> and Ducange</seg></note>
        <note type="editorNote" subtype="footnote" xml:id="Ine_28.attnote.fn.7" n="7" source="#attenborough"><bibl><biblScope unit="page">44</biblScope></bibl><label>he</label><seg type="original" xml:lang="en">H* &amp; B.</seg><note type="remark" resp="#claude">The number 7 is printed 2 times on the page (28, 28), with one footnote.</note></note>
        <note type="editorNote" subtype="footnote" xml:id="Ine_28.attnote.fn.7-2" n="7" source="#attenborough"><bibl><biblScope unit="page">44</biblScope></bibl><label>he</label><seg type="original" xml:lang="en">H* &amp; B.</seg><note type="remark" resp="#claude">The number 7 is printed 2 times on the page (28, 28), with one footnote.</note></note>
        <note type="editorNote" subtype="endnote" xml:id="Ine_28.attnote.n.1" n="1" source="#attenborough"><bibl><biblScope unit="page">186</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="en"><hi rend="italic">i.e.</hi> his captor.</seg></note>
